{"parentUuid":"146b727e-5e47-444a-937f-2144f3019dff","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fb64cbf9-b60e-4920-bc4f-b051258cb529","agentId":"a7676847d82e04abb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BQebLXHnqpM4bRefTDu5WJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1902:    def _power_pole_shell_distance(\n1903-        self,\n1904-        domain: ModeRectDomain,\n1905-        x_val: int,\n1906-        y_val: int,\n1907-    ) -> Tuple[int, int]:\n1908-        dx = min(int(x_val - domain.x_min), int(domain.x_max - x_val))\n1909-        dy = min(int(y_val - domain.y_min), int(domain.y_max - y_val))\n1910-        return int(dx), int(dy)\n1911-\n1912-    def _power_pole_family_sort_key(self, family_name: str) -> Tuple[Any, ...]:\n1913-        template_order = sorted(self.owner._exact_powered_template_demands())\n1914-        coefficients = self._power_pole_family_coefficients.get(str(family_name), {})\n1915-        coefficient_key = tuple(-int(coefficients.get(str(tpl), 0)) for tpl in template_order)\n1916-        return (\n1917-            coefficient_key,\n1918-            -int(self._power_pole_family_pose_counts.get(str(family_name), 0)),\n1919-            str(family_name),\n1920-        )\n1921-\n1922-    def _prepare_power_pole_families(self) -> None:\n1923-        self._power_pole_family_name_by_int = {}\n1924-        self._power_pole_family_coefficients = {}\n1925-        self._power_pole_family_id_by_pose_idx = {}\n1926-        self._power_pole_family_pose_counts = {}\n1927-        self._power_pole_family_order = []"}]},"uuid":"d739e32b-8832-4528-b9b1-93dfb055c2e1","timestamp":"2026-05-08T00:48:23.443Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"146b727e-5e47-444a-937f-2144f3019dff","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d739e32b-8832-4528-b9b1-93dfb055c2e1","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a7676847d82e04abb","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_015HGxiVv8xEtbFbX8FTWPEA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have all I need. Let me also check whether `slot.active=False -> slot.x = pole_domain.x_min, slot.y = pole_domain.y_min` already implicitly forces dx/dy → and through them d_lo/d_hi.\n\nLooking at line 2831-2832:\n```python\nself.model.Add(slot.x == int(pole_domain.x_min)).OnlyEnforceIf(slot.active.Not())\nself.model.Add(slot.y == int(pole_domain.y_min)).OnlyEnforceIf(slot.active.Not())\n```\n\nWhen `slot.active = False`:\n- `slot.x = pole_domain.x_min`, `slot.y = pole_domain.y_min`\n- `_add_power_pole_shell_distance_constraints` is **unconditional** (no `OnlyEnforceIf`):\n  - `dx = min(slot.x - x_min, x_max - slot.x) = min(0, x_max - x_min) = 0` (linear_minmax) or via element table at `slot.x = x_min` → `0` (lookup branch)\n  - `dy = 0` similarly\n- `d_lo = min(dx, dy) = 0`, `d_hi = max(dx, dy) = 0` (unconditional MinEquality/MaxEquality at lines 2847-2848)\n\nSo when inactive, `(d_lo, d_hi) = (0, 0)` is already **forced unconditionally** by the unconditional propagation chain (slot.x → dx → d_lo). The blueprint's claim \"d_lo / d_hi has no inactive enforcement\" is technically true at the `OnlyEnforceIf` grep level, but the values **are pinned to (0, 0) via transitive propagation**.\n\nNow, the critical question: **Is (0, 0) one of the real `shell_pair_rows`?**\n\n`(0, 0)` corresponds to a pole sitting at the corner `(x_min, y_min)` of its mode_rect domain. From `_power_pole_shell_distance`: `dx = min(x_val - x_min, x_max - x_val)`. If `x_val = x_min`, then `dx = 0`. Similarly for `y`. So `(0, 0)` is a real legitimate shell pair (a pole at the corner of its valid placement domain) — and **almost certainly appears in `pair_to_family_name`** because the shell-lookup family construction iterates over actual pose enumeration, and corner placements are real poses.\n\nThis means **`(d_lo, d_hi) = (0, 0)` is a real row** — it is a valid shell-pair for some family. Setting `sentinel = (0, 0)` would collide.\n\nLet me now reason about the actual sentinel-row construction safety."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":794,"cache_read_input_tokens":31547,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":794,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CapBUibfGwviXgpeGHp1G","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"492dc588-c950-43e5-97ab-816fd3fd9037","timestamp":"2026-05-08T00:48:38.947Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
